flowchart TD
    Call["BPF program calls a function<br/><b>does:</b> source names helper or __ksym kfunc<br/><b>why next:</b> loader/verifier must resolve callable target<br/><b>state:</b> call site in BPF bytecode"]
    Kind{"which mechanism?"}
    HelperID["helper path<br/><b>does:</b> compiler encodes BPF_FUNC_* enum id<br/><b>why next:</b> verifier has per-program-type helper proto table<br/><b>state:</b> stable UAPI helper number"]
    HelperVerify["helper verification<br/><b>does:</b> checks arg/return types against bpf_func_proto<br/><b>why next:</b> runtime can dispatch through helper table<br/><b>state:</b> allowed helper call"]
    HelperRun["helper runtime<br/><b>does:</b> calls fixed kernel helper implementation<br/><b>state:</b> UAPI semantics remain stable across kernels"]
    Ksym["kfunc path<br/><b>does:</b> libbpf records symbol name with __ksym relocation<br/><b>why next:</b> target kernel BTF must contain matching function<br/><b>state:</b> unresolved-by-name call"]
    KVerify["kfunc verification<br/><b>does:</b> checks BTF signature, flags, acquire/release rules<br/><b>why next:</b> direct kernel call is safe only with type proof<br/><b>state:</b> typed kfunc call or load failure"]
    KRun["kfunc runtime<br/><b>does:</b> calls in-kernel function directly<br/><b>state:</b> not UAPI; availability can vary by kernel"]

    Call --> Kind
    Kind -->|frozen UAPI helper| HelperID --> HelperVerify --> HelperRun
    Kind -->|BTF-exposed kfunc| Ksym --> KVerify --> KRun

